It is Saturday morning and I am helping in the café.
Elif and I are working together behind the till.
A customer orders a coffee.
"That is three euros, please," I say.
He pays and takes his coffee.
"Do you have a guest WiFi here?" he asks me.
"Yes, of course," I answer.
"The network is called Cafe-Gast."
"The password is on the small card here by the till."
He takes out his phone and types.
"Unfortunately it is not connecting," the customer says after a moment.
"Normally that takes a little while," I explain.
"Turn the WiFi on your phone off and on again."
"Usually it works the second time."
"A webpage is then opened automatically," I explain further.
"There you simply have to click on accept."
He tries it one more time and nods, smiling.
"Now I am online, thank you very much!" he says.
He goes to his table, and Elif grins at me.
